Information about the Folderstructure 

         ╔═══ PostScript
Radar ═══╬═══ Renders
         ╚═══ Compas

PostScript: When Python Turtle saves an Render img, the instructed Turtle operations are saved here by using GhostScript for image display and debuging purposes.

Renders: Generated images from RadarDrawing.cs are saved here for display in ConsoleRadar.py, a new Render will overwrite the previeus Render.

Compas: The Compas is an Overlay over the Render so the user can view the heading when rendered on screen (when is not rotated is always T, R will rotate this overlay)

PostScript and Renders are deleted afther closing the aplication to ensure optimal performance and optimization for the next operation.

Note: this was used in legacy code, PostScript en Renders is now saved in RAM memory, Compas data is is still required for radar rendering components.
